{"title":"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. Prove that the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae4ca4be8d2099b3571fa08533bcc760ef85615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^{n+1} - z^n - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> has a complex root with modulus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e3acd481bacb78f324773254902e3a08d848f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Divide each side of the equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> of the side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equal segments. Through these division points, draw lines parallel to the other two sides, partitioning the triangle into small triangles. The vertices of these small triangles are called nodes. A real number is placed at every node.\n</p><p>It is known that:\n</p>\n<ol><li>The numbers placed at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />, respectively;</li>\n<li>In every rhombus formed by two minimal triangles sharing a common side, the sums of the numbers at the two pairs of opposite vertices are equal.</li></ol>\n<p>Find:\n</p>\n<ol><li>The shortest distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> between the node carrying the maximum number and the node carrying the minimum number;</li>\n<li>The total sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of the numbers at all nodes.</li></ol>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a sports competition, every pair of contestants plays exactly one match, and every match has a definite winner and loser. Outstanding contestants are determined by the following rule:\n</p><p>Contestant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is defined to be an outstanding contestant if, for any other contestant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> beats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, or there exists some contestant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> beats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> beats <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Prove that if there is exactly one outstanding contestant under this rule, then this contestant beats every other contestant.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Five points are placed arbitrarily inside an equilateral triangle of area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that within this equilateral triangle, one can construct three equilateral triangles covering the five points. The sides of these three new equilateral triangles are parallel to the sides of the original triangle, and the sum of their areas is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27eb4ed7d163216ec447f745dd2d914135fcb713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8ee494a33436b15ad1f25ad94a88a2cb6d7fea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 A_2 A_3 A_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> be a tetrahedron. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390c718c7b72b05922b9bc7fff77d3615a1057f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1, S_2, S_3, S_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> be spheres with centres at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c42ee5b0fb229e8708441e6be436a8c0082752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, A_2, A_3, A_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />, respectively, and these spheres are pairwise tangent. Suppose there exists a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that a sphere centred at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is tangent to all of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390c718c7b72b05922b9bc7fff77d3615a1057f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1, S_2, S_3, S_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />, and a sphere centred at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to every edge of the tetrahedron. Prove that the tetrahedron is regular.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> distinct positive even integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct positive odd integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/75861193dfa356e5aa64e170d6991a8137d4295c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1987$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Among all such pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b7e4c455672c30d743cce7506408a40cb68129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, find the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8b4daa6cd90b60ecc6e762fc24281e5bc5c12d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3m+4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"15\" />. Prove your answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA)\">1987 CMO(CHINA)</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_CMO(CHINA)\" title=\"1986 CMO(CHINA)\">1986 CMO(CHINA)</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_CMO(CHINA)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1988 CMO(CHINA) (page does not exist)\">1988 CMO(CHINA)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_CMO(CHINA)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 CMO(CHINA) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CMO(CHINA)_Problems_and_Solutions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions\"> All CMO(CHINA) Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043216\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 231/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 980/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 74/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/10